  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-02-25T18:30:27.803Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Having a person in your instance blocked causes a disruptive disconnect between your experience and the experience of other people around you. It's confusing and frustrating for a person to be present for some but non-existent for others.\nPlease redesign the blocking system to improve this.\nMy suggestions:\n- Render a mute representation of the blocked person in world space. This can be a ghost avatar, an icon, something unobtrusive (see attached image example).\n- The representation of the blocked person should NOT appear at all within the blocker's personal space bubble. This guarantees against virtual physical harassment.\n- Show when the blocked person is talking on their microphone without hearing their voice or what they're saying. This is analogous to how Discord handles blocked users (see image).\n\nRelated but different: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/option-to-draw-an-outline-where-a-blocked-person-is",
